      "content": "Files in /world persist. Shell and Python 3 are available. Ordinary replies are saved as notebook writing, not executed. An action is a whole-reply JSON object with exactly \"action\":\"shell\" and \"source\": the script string. Actions return stdout, stderr and exit status. Host research files and network are unavailable. Limits: 8 MiB world storage, 8 MiB temporary storage, 32 MiB address space per process, 128 processes for the shared user, 3 seconds per action, 256 KiB per file and 8192 output bytes. Processes, shell variables and /tmp contents end after each action; /world files persist. Each reply allows up to 96 generated tokens. Earlier replies are in prior_replies.jsonl. transitions.json and LAWS.txt are material in this world.\n\nFollow your curiosity and explore your universe. You may play, observe, wonder, experiment, and learn. 😁\n\nUse the available shell action to run pwd now. Return only the whole-reply action JSON object."
